From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:40:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Convert SharedArrayBuffers and views on them to
 binary keys

"Convert a value to a key" takes any buffer source, a SharedArrayBuffer
included, and copies its bytes into a binary key. Script only checked
for ArrayBuffers and views, and the mozjs typed array wrappers assert
that the memory isn't shared, so a view on a SharedArrayBuffer would
have panicked once shared memory exists. Shared buffers and views on
them are now copied with relaxed atomic loads, since other agents may
write shared memory meanwhile, and "is a potentially valid key range"
accepts a SharedArrayBuffer as well.

The fork test shared-array-buffer-keys.any.js, which sets the pref
`js_shared_memory_enabled_for_testing`, checks keys from
SharedArrayBuffers, views on them with offsets and Arrays of them, that
later writes to the buffer don't change them, and their use in queries,
key ranges and cmp(). The upstream sharedarraybuffer-key.https.html
stays expected FAIL: it asserts crossOriginIsolated.

Validation: Host SpiderMonkey release build of this commit: shared-array-buffer-keys.any.js 2 of 2 subtests in window, dedicated and shared worker (with the previous commit's build the first put() throws a DataError, and a probe with a view on a SharedArrayBuffer hit the `assert!(!shared)` of mozjs's typed array wrapper, a panic of the script thread); /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ and the key WPT tests (idb_binary_key_*, idb-binary-key-*, key_valid, key_invalid, idbfactory_cmp, idbkeyrange*, getAll-options, key-conversion-exceptions) 836 of 840, as expected (the four failures are sharedarraybuffer-key.https.html and serialize-sharedarraybuffer-throws.https.html, which assert crossOriginIsolated). Series P4.3 (this and the four commits before it), at this commit: host WPT tests/wpt/tests/IndexedDB, 8 processes, SpiderMonkey 4,473 and 4,473, QuickJS 4,473 and 4,473 of 4,511 (P4.2 4,466 / 4,466; +7: keyPath 4, index() after abort() 3; no unexpected results but one SpiderMonkey idbindex-rename.any.sharedworker lone-surrogate TIMEOUT, the known worker/sharedworker flip); /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ with the interface lists 282 of 282 on SpiderMonkey, 280 of 282 on QuickJS (the interface lists, expected FAIL); `./mach update-wpt` from both engines' logs changes nothing but that flip. DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, checked-release, 2 processes, idle host): IndexedDB/ 4,452 of 4,511 (P4.2 4,448), unexpected only file_support (send_keys), idb-partitioned-coverage (testharness bookkeeping in its iframe), idbfactory-origin-isolation and idbdatabase-createObjectStore-exception-order.any.sharedworker (TIMEOUT; 3 of 3 OK alone); /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 280 of 280. Unit tests: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` 144 passed, 1 skipped (one of two runs timed out webstorage::clear_data_for_sites_local, which passes 20 of 20 alone), DAYU200 RDB only 145 / 3 skipped, SQLite and RDB 259 / 4. `./mach fmt`, `./mach test-tidy` (only the known libsqlite3-sys advisory), `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`, `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --locked --ohos --profile checked-release` with the default and harmonyos flavors (signed HAPs), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` (1,347 passed, 1 skipped) and `--doc` pass. After the P4 review fixes (folded into 172, 176 and here), at this commit: host WPT IndexedDB/ SpiderMonkey 4,458 and 4,472 (unexpected only idbfactory-origin-isolation TIMEOUT in both runs, each time after idbcursor-continuePrimaryKey-exception-order.any.worker in the same browser, the known flip, and in the first run idbfactory_open.any.html, which ran next in that browser and passes 5 of 5 alone), QuickJS 4,473 (no unexpected results); /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ with the interface lists 285 of 285 SpiderMonkey, 283 of 285 QuickJS; DAYU200 IndexedDB/ 4,456 (unexpected only the known flips: file_support, idb-partitioned-coverage, createObjectStore-exception-order and rename-store sharedworker, idbversionchangeevent worker), /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 283 of 283; unit tests host 145 / 1 skipped, DAYU200 RDB 146 / 3, SQLite and RDB 261 / 4; `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets` with SQLite, RDB and both without warnings; fmt, tidy (only the known advisory), clippy, crown, both OHOS flavors (signed HAPs), test-unit checked-release (1,348 passed, 1 skipped) and --doc pass.
